        // Page Content
        .container-fluid.p-0

            // About
            section#about.resume-section
                .resume-section-content
                    h1.mb-0
                        | Victor Soto 
                        span.text-primary Alexander
                    .subheading.mb-5
                        | Mexico City · (+52) 55-6676-9310 ·
                        a(href='mailto:alexandervictor550@gmail.com') alexandervictor550@gmail.com
                    p.lead.mb-5
                        | System Development Engineer with a software- and support-engineering background, specializing in operational tooling, automation, and diagnostics for large-scale publishing systems. I build AI-assisted workflows, automate away repetitive toil, and turn one-off fixes into version-controlled, reusable tooling that scales across a team. I work primarily in Java, Python, and Bash, and I care about reliable systems and clean, maintainable solutions.
                    .mb-5
                        a.btn.btn-primary(href='assets/pdf/Victor_Soto_Alexander_CV.pdf', target='_blank')
                            i.fas.fa-download.me-2
                            | Download CV (PDF)
                    .social-icons
                        a.social-icon(href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/soto-alexander/' target='_blank')
                            i.fab.fa-linkedin-in
                        a.social-icon(href='https://github.com/victoralexander132' target='_blank')
                            i.fab.fa-github

            hr.m-0

            // Experience
            section#experience.resume-section
               .resume-section-content
                    h2.mb-5 Experience

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 System Development Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Amazon · promoted from Support Engineer III
                            p Automation- and tooling-focused engineer on the KDP/POD publisher-support organization, building systems that reduce operational load across the team.
                            ul
                                li Built an AI agent/skill that automates publisher content-eligibility diagnostics, cutting resolution of tickets that previously took ~30 minutes each (~10/week) and saving the team ~20 hours per month.
                                li Reduced manual toil by ~20 hours/month by replacing a manual financial-reporting process for publishers with scripted and AI-assisted workflows.
                                li Migrated ~100 wiki pages to documentation-as-code (version-controlled Markdown), making SOPs reviewable in git and easily consumable by AI agents.
                                li Authored 30+ operational runbooks and contributed to 300+, standardizing recurring-ticket resolution across the team.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary June 2026 - Present

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Support Engineer III
                            .subheading.mb-3 Amazon
                            p Sustained the reliability of publisher-reporting infrastructure while building automation to shrink the team's operational burden.
                            ul
                                li Triaged and resolved production trouble tickets over 29 months across 4 resolver groups, maintaining 90%+ SLA compliance.
                                li Owned on-call for the Kindle publisher-reporting backend, resolving 90%+ of pages without escalation.
                                li Reduced repeat self-service marketing tickets by identifying documentation gaps, updating content, and assigning clear ownership for its upkeep.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary January 2024 - June 2026

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Software Engineer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Unosquare
                            p Built and maintained software solutions for US-based clients using Java and SQL databases in a Scrum / continuous-delivery workflow.
                            ul
                                li Managed database schema changes using SQL, ensuring data consistency across multiple systems.
                                li Built and maintained API test suites for RESTful services using ReadyAPI.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary August 2022 - December 2023

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Junior Java Fullstack Developer
                            .subheading.mb-3 Generation Mexico
                            p Completed an intensive, hands-on Java fullstack bootcamp — building and testing web applications with Java and Spring Boot, designing relational databases with MySQL, and implementing front-end interfaces with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary March 2022 - June 2022

